  "section_notes": "S1 is strict: 24-hour reporting for a broad set of incidents and 5-business-day customer notice. S2 weakens the 5% cap to an 8% market ceiling, with only corrective action above 5% and no customer access to per-model failure rates. S3 delays new-unit shut-off to 3 years and allows a 6-year retrofit with feasibility escape; S4 requires built-in suppression from 36 months; S5 has an 8/100k review trigger but leaves recall to regulator discretion and uses 'promptly' for notices."
